<p>In a mixture of helium, oxygen, and methane in a 2.00 L container, the partial pressures of He and O<sub>2</sub> are 13.6 kPa and 29.2 kPa, respectively, and the total pressure inside the container is 95.4 kPa. What is the partial pressure of methane? If the methane is ignited to initiate its combustion with oxygen and the system is then cooled to the original temperature of 30&deg;C, what is the final pressure inside the container (in kilopascals)?</p>

